  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 239 AM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nMuch cooler air moves in behind the front and Thursday evening sees \ntemperatures tumble into the 40s and 50s. As the front moves \nsouth, the bulk of the rain also moves to the south, but high \nrain chances will exist over much of the CWA with the exception of\nparts of SE NM. An extension of the Flood Watch may be needed for\nsome areas south of I-10 on Friday as another round of rain may \nbe seen. Fall like temperatures continue through Saturday as highs\nstruggle to reach 60F and overnight lows settle into the low to \nmid 40s. \n\nThe area begins to dry out late Friday and into Saturday with rain \nchances decreasing below 10% for much of the region. By Sunday, \nhighs reach back into the 70s with lows in the 50s. A warm up back \nto normal continues through early next week. \n\n-Stickney",
